# One line-ending convention for the whole repository, whatever each machine is
# configured to do.
#
# The repository stores text as LF. Git for Windows checks out CRLF by default
# (core.autocrlf=true), which is fine on its own - but a clone made without that
# setting, e.g. from WSL or Linux, then sees every CRLF file as modified and a
# single "git add -A" would rewrite the whole tree. This file makes normalisation
# a property of the project instead of a property of each clone's config.
* text=auto

# Docker runs these through a shell inside the image; CR at the end of a RUN line
# is a real bug there, so pin them regardless of platform.
*.docker                                text eol=lf
tourcalc.experiment.docker.from-scratch  text eol=lf

# Never convert anything inside these.
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.svg   text
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
